cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dictionary, cite it as below, and also cite the taxonomy it approximates (Danescu-Niculescu-Mizil et al., 2013)."
title: "TASS Politeness Markers"
version: "1.0.0"
type: dataset
license: CC-BY-4.0
authors:
  - family-names: Leith
    given-names: Alex P.
    affiliation: "SIM DAD LLC"
abstract: >
  Fifteen politeness-strategy marker categories (gratitude, deference, greeting, apology,
  hedge, please, indirection, first- and second-person address, modality, factuality,
  affirmation, negation, and related strategies). A lexical and phrase-level approximation
  of the politeness strategy taxonomy of Danescu-Niculescu-Mizil, Sudhof, Jurafsky,
  Leskovec, and Potts (2013), not a reimplementation of that paper's trained classifier.
  Report it as an approximation.
url: "https://github.com/SIM-DAD/tass-lexicons"
references:
  - type: conference-paper
    title: "A computational approach to politeness with application to social factors"
    authors:
      - family-names: Danescu-Niculescu-Mizil
        given-names: Cristian
      - family-names: Sudhof
        given-names: Moritz
      - family-names: Jurafsky
        given-names: Dan
      - family-names: Leskovec
        given-names: Jure
      - family-names: Potts
        given-names: Christopher
    year: 2013
    conference:
      name: "ACL 2013"
